    <briefdescription>
<para>A single chunk of a snapshot suitable for wire transfer. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Large snapshots are split into fixed-size chunks. Each chunk carries a SHA-256 checksum of its own payload so that the receiver can detect corruption or a truncated transfer without waiting for the final chunk. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
